<title>UK: BOE's George says aims to pre-empt inflation.</title>
<headline>BOE's George says aims to pre-empt inflation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The short term outlook for inflation is encouraging but the Bank of England is more concerned about containing inflationary pressures that may be building up in the longer term, central bank Governor Eddie George said.</p>
<p>&quot;That's what we're about, pre-emptive action to moderate the pace of the upswing to a sustainable pace rather than leave it too little, too late,&quot; George said on BBC radio 4.</p>
</text>
